From: MakOS Project <makos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] media: use auxv AArch64 CPU detection on MakOS

MakOS supplies ELF auxv HWCAP/HWCAP2 through musl. Reuse libvpx's generic
AArch64 auxv detector without identifying MakOS as Linux.

diff --git a/media/libvpx/libvpx/vpx_ports/aarch64_cpudetect.c b/media/libvpx/libvpx/vpx_ports/aarch64_cpudetect.c
--- a/media/libvpx/libvpx/vpx_ports/aarch64_cpudetect.c
+++ b/media/libvpx/libvpx/vpx_ports/aarch64_cpudetect.c
@@ -120,7 +120,7 @@ int arm_cpu_caps(void) {
   return flags;
 }
 
-#elif defined(__linux__)  // end defined(VPX_USE_ANDROID_CPU_FEATURES)
+#elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__makos__)  // end VPX_USE_ANDROID_CPU_FEATURES
 
 #include <sys/auxv.h>
 
